<ui:UXML xmlns:ui="UnityEngine.UIElements" xmlns:uie="UnityEditor.UIElements" editor-extension-mode="False">
    <ui:VisualElement name="step-2-cutouts" style="flex-grow: 1;">
        <ui:Label text="Room Creation..." display-tooltip-when-elided="true" name="step-header" style="flex-direction: row; flex-grow: 0; height: auto; font-size: 20px; -unity-text-align: upper-center; flex-shrink: 1; -unity-font-style: bold; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-bottom: 4px;"/>
        <ui:Label text="- Open the Room Creator via the menu option &quot;ExPresS XR &gt; Rooms... &gt; Room Creator&quot;. Create a room with the size (5, 3, 4) and Material Preset &quot;Exhibition&quot;. This will create an exhibition room with dimensions 5m x 3m x 4m (width x height x depth). This dimension is the default when calling &quot;ExPresS XR &gt; Rooms... &gt; Create Default Exhibition Room&quot;. - Add the window at &quot;Assets/ExPresS XR/Tutorial Assets/Room/Window Big Plain.prefab&quot; and set it&#39;s position to (0, 1.2, 1.95) intersecting the wall. - Switch to the &quot;ProBuilder Context&quot; (if not done already) by locating the context menu first. It is usually docked on the left side of the Scene View. Here click on the dropdown displaying the wireframe of a cube at the top of the context menu and select &quot;ProBuilder&quot;. - Select ProBuilder&#39;s newly appeared EdgeSelection-Mode in the header bar of the Scene View. - On the wall intersecting the window, select one edge then right-click and select &quot;ProBuilder Select &gt; Insert Edge Loop&quot;. This will create an edge wrapping around the room orthogonal to the selected edge. Move the edge loops to intersect the window frame using it&#39;s gimbal. - Repeat with the other three edges. This will enclose the wall inside of the window with edges forming a new face which now must be deleted. - Change the ProBuilder&#39;s FaceSelection-Mode next to the EdgeSelection-Mode. Select the face and delete it by right-clicking again and selecting &quot;ProBuilder Select &gt; Insert Edge Loop&quot; or by simply pressing the Backspace-Button. - Repeat for the second window. You do not need to add horizontal edge loops, as the one&#39;s from the first window are already placed at the correct height. - Switch back to the Object Context using the Context Menu on the left to be able to select GameObjects normally again." display-tooltip-when-elided="true" name="step-description" style="flex-grow: 1; white-space: normal;"/>
    </ui:VisualElement>
    <ui:VisualElement name="controls-view" style="flex-direction: row; justify-content: flex-end;">
        <ui:Button text="Back" display-tooltip-when-elided="true" name="back-button"/>
        <ui:Button text="Next" display-tooltip-when-elided="true" name="next-button"/>
    </ui:VisualElement>
</ui:UXML>
